## How it works

Paths are resampled within each arm, once per replicate, and every metric,
stratum and period is evaluated on the same resample. Any quantity built from
the rows of one replicate — a ratio of two metrics, the difference between two
periods, the empirical fraction of positive draws (not a posterior probability or p-value) — therefore preserves the joint dependence of those estimates, provided paths
are independent analysis units. A percentile interval is available only when the
statistic is defined in every replicate and has nonzero bootstrap variation;
dropping undefined draws would silently change the sampling distribution.
The replicates match the ones behind the ratio rows of
[`get_ab_test`](/docs/tools/get-ab-test) for the same `random_state`.
Fixed horizons and since-assignment periods require an explicit, exclusive
`observation_end` logging cutoff, just as the scorecard does. The same seed, data
and configuration reproduce the draw; numerical draws from the pre-integration
implementation are not a compatibility promise.

Contrasts additionally require identical measurement eligibility across the
contrasted periods; changing missingness rejects even with a common roster.
Requests are capped at 1,000,000 draws and 10,000,000 replicate-by-contribution
entries. Numeric overflow raises. These are advanced approximate summaries;
large B cannot recover unobserved tail information or repair dependent units.

Replicate rows carry no `reading`: the sentence that reads each metric is on the
scorecard row of `get_ab_test`.

